  message: "DONE in PR #2188 (dev 1bf655d034, commit perf(sketch): the config extraction reads the shipped probe embeddings). The item offered two fixes; the first was taken: sketch_embeddings.probe_embeddings(name, model, dim) is the one reader of all four shipped arrays, guarded by a sha256 digest of the model name and the probe texts (PROBE_DIGESTS in _embedding_data) and by the row width; when either guard fails the model encodes the probes as before. FILED REPRO RE-RUN on dev 1bf655d034 (fake encoder patched over _load_embedding_model, _extract_config_embedding called twice on a 2-file fixture, discovery stubbed): with a 768-wide fake the encode batches are [6, 6], the repository's own chunks only; the item recorded [41, 127, 5, 12, 41, 127, 5, 12]. With a 64-wide fake the batches are [6, 41, 127, 12, 6, 41, 127, 12]: by design, 768-wide shipped rows cannot be scored against a 64-wide model. The two getters without a caller are removed (grep over packages, scripts and tests: 0 hits). The duplicate lists in sketch.py are removed (ANSWER_PATTERNS and BIG_PICTURE_QUESTIONS are assigned only in sketch_embeddings.py). REAL MODEL: stored vs encoded-now cosine 1.000000 for every probe of all four sets; _extract_config_embedding on 21 real repositories returns the same 548 lines in the same order before and after, 103.7 s to 85.9 s for the 21 calls (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/slow_tests_11142026: probe_check_out.txt, config_before.json, config_after.json). Pinned by packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_probe_embeddings.py (12 cases); mutation controls: digest check always true, 3 fail; width check dropped, 2 fail. NOT DONE and not part of this item: _discover_config_files_embedding still encodes the known config file names for the repository's languages on every call; no embedding of them is shipped."  # 5b6e
